@page "/support"
@{
    Layout = "/Pages/Shared/_PublicLayout.cshtml";
    ViewData["Title"] = "Support";
    const string contactEmail = "dmitry.shapar@gmail.com";
}

<h1>DeyeSolar support</h1>
<p>For help with the mobile app, the hosted service, or privacy requests, email:</p>
<p><a class="contact-link" href="mailto:@contactEmail">@contactEmail</a></p>

<h2>What to include</h2>
<ul>
    <li>The app version, phone model, and operating system version.</li>
    <li>The server address you are connecting to.</li>
    <li>What you tried, what you expected, and the error message or approximate time of the issue.</li>
    <li>A screenshot if useful, with personal details and credentials removed.</li>
</ul>
<p>Do not send passwords, session tokens, Deye application secrets, or Shelly authorization keys.
    Support will not ask for your Apple account password.</p>

<h2>Connecting to a server</h2>
<p>DeyeSolar requires an existing account on a configured DeyeSolar server. The mobile app does not
    create accounts. For sign-in credentials or password help, contact the operator of your server.
    The default hosted server is <a href="https://solar.dshapar.com">solar.dshapar.com</a>.</p>
<p>If the app cannot load data, check your internet connection and server address, then try again.
    The server must have working Deye or Shelly connection settings for the relevant devices and readings.</p>

<h2>Device control and automation</h2>
<p>Device commands and enabled rules can change the state of connected Shelly devices. Before changing
    them, confirm which device you are controlling and that you are authorized to operate the installation.
    If a device or installation needs attention, contact its operator.</p>

<h2>Privacy</h2>
<p>Read the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> for information about stored account details,
    connection settings, installation data, and how to request access, correction, or deletion.</p>
